  "hazards": [
    "6 of 30 subjects fell out of the room front under gravity settle — their authored positions sit past the shell's open +z floor edge (floor footprint ends at z=0.95), so there is no support under them. Impulse-gravity placement cannot place an object with no support below it.",
    "2 of 30 authored subjects rest on the floor; the other 28 are wall/ceiling/surface-mounted or floating. Under gravity settle 22 of them fall to the floor and 6 fall out the front — impulse placement is only defined for support-resting objects.",
    "equipmentPlacements carry position but no dimensions in the scene manifest (ecg_cart_equipment, iv_stand_equipment), and the equipment GLBs are gitignored — equipment penetration is not measured here; sizing them would be invention."
  ],
  "rationale": "Bake-off ran offline in Rapier 0.19.3 (dynamic + applyImpulse + CCD + locked rotation + contact settle; 30 subjects, 297 steps/subject avg, 900 max). Control worst penetration 0.0000 m — the authored triples already avoid the solid shell (their known defects are floating and object-overlap, a different class than wall penetration). Treatment worst 0.0011 m and 6 subjects fell out of the open front. Impulse placement settles floor-standing bodies to ~1 mm resting penetration (Rapier contact tolerance), ties the control on penetration, and cannot express the 28 mounted/floating subjects — 22 fall to the floor, 6 escape the open front. On this population the treatment loses on scope and cost without a penetration win, so it is not a drop-in for the authored triple.",
  "verdictNote": "shipped cast scenarios enumerated: 14; measured population is the 30 scene-manifest room props of ed_chest_pain_priority_v1 (the only station whose room props ship through the runtime-bundles builder; the factory presets author 16 room props in a non-exported helper and the other stations ship none by design, #149). Control holds 0 room penetration; the treatment ties it, drops mounted/unsupported props, and adds cost — reject, not adopt."
}
